---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const b='/equipment/08-07/',uc='https://cnm2.ucdavis.edu/equipment/evg-810-plasma-activation',vendor='https://www.evgroup.com/products/bonding/fusion-and-hybrid-bonding-systems/evg810-lt/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="EVG 810 surface activation station" description="Inspect a metric bench model and track the simulated activation record of an inert coupon face." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="evg810"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-07/">← Equipment 08-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#evg-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">08-07 / PACKAGING · SURFACE RECORDS</p><h2>Activation belongs to one face</h2><p class="eq-lede">With face A exposed, close the virtual lid and record a simulated event. Then open it and flip the coupon. Face B has not been treated, and neither face has a bond-strength measurement.</p></header>
<div class="e-cols"><section><h3>EVG 810 single chamber</h3><canvas id="evg-model" aria-label="Orbitable EVG 810, chamber, coupon and console"></canvas><p id="evg-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="evg-front">Whole station / reset view</button><button id="evg-chamber">Chamber close-up</button><button id="evg-rear">Rear view</button><p>Click the metal lid or colored wafer face in the chamber close-up. Clicking the monitor invokes the same simulated record action as the form.</p></section>
<section><h3>Face eligibility exercise</h3><p id="evg-face"></p><label>Teaching compatibility rule <select id="evg-material"><option value="qualified">Synthetic Si/SiO₂ stack (qualified rule)</option><option value="unknown">Unknown inert stack (not qualified)</option></select></label><p><button id="evg-lid">Close chamber lid</button><button id="evg-load">Remove coupon</button><button id="evg-flip">Flip coupon</button><button id="evg-record">Record simulated activation</button><button id="evg-reset">Restore example</button></p><p id="evg-status" role="status"></p><p>No physical process settings, treatment recipe or measured surface chemistry. The record is a hypothetical annotation that you can inspect and export.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Face ledger</h3><p id="evg-rev"></p><div class="e-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Face</th><th>Activation prerequisite</th><th>Recorded UTC</th><th>Bond strength</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td id="evg-A"></td><td id="evg-Atime"></td><td>Not measured</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td id="evg-B"></td><td id="evg-Btime"></td><td>Not measured</td></tr></tbody></table></div><button id="evg-export">Download face-history JSON</button><p>Separate surface IDs, material rule, simulated event type, assigned UTC timestamp and revision are preserved. <a href={b+'example.json'}>Example export</a>. Satisfying this rule does not mean that bonding is complete or guaranteed.</p></section>
<section id="evg-evidence"><h3>Reference and checks</h3><p>Original model of the <a href={uc}>EVG 810 installation at UC Davis CNM2</a>: separate accessory rack, central fenced chamber and offset console. The <a href={vendor}>EVG810 LT product family</a> documents single-chamber manual specimen handling and a nominal 50–200 mm wafer size option; this build chooses a 150 mm virtual specimen within that option, without claiming that the pictured Davis configuration has that exact holder. The cabinet, chamber travel and auxiliary details have no sourced dimensions and are inferred.</p><div class="e-cols"><figure><img src={b+'station.webp'} alt="Original EVG 810 whole station rendering"/><figcaption>Original rendered rack, glass enclosure and console. Compare the UC Davis installation photo.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={b+'chamber.webp'} alt="Original close-up of the raised chamber and 150 mm coupon"/><figcaption>Original teaching chamber close-up, not a photograph. The blue and lavender face markers are simulation-only.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Register verification: identify A and B by stable surface IDs. After recording on A, A satisfies the activation prerequisite; B remains unrelated. Flip and optionally record separately on B. Both exports keep strength null. A closed empty chamber, an open lid or an unqualified teaching material rejects a record.</p><p><a href={b+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={b+'evg810.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={b+'eligibility.mjs'}>Pure state actions and output contract</a> · <a href={b+'vr.json'}>VR bounds and model budget</a>. No headset or process validation is claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-07/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#evg810 .e-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#evg810 section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#evg810 :is(select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#evg810 button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#evg810 button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#evg-model{display:block;width:100%;height:350px;touch-action:none}#evg810 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#evg810 figure img{width:100%}#evg810 .e-scroll{overflow:auto}#evg810 table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#evg810 td,#evg810 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#evg810 .e-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#evg-model{height:285px}}</style>
